The perimeter of a rectangle is calculated by the formula P = 2(length + width).  In this case, the length is 6 miles and the width is 1.5 miles.  So, the perimeter of the park is 2(6 + 1.5) = 2(7.5) = 15 miles.

Gary walks a distance of 15 miles at a speed of 3 miles per hour. Time = Distance / Speed.  Therefore, the time Gary spends walking is 15 miles / 3 miles/hour = 5 hours.

\boxed{5}
